: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<div id=\"itinerary\" class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-content gdlr-core-js \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-container clearfix gdlr-core-container\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>Enjoy the huge amusement park with water slides, splash pads, water playground, and other recreational bathing and swimming environments for all ages, even for infants, open year around with accommodation in unique and romantic over water rooms and bungalows which can be reached by gondola</p>\r\n<p>The park features a full-day of fun for the entire family, whether you make a splash in the cool blue waves, take a thrilling ride down any of our 32 watersides, or just float around the lazy river. Aqua Park has over a million gallons of water and 30 acres of action packed adventure with something for everyone. The park is fully staffed lifeguards to ensure safe fun for everyone. The park provides personal flotation devices at no charge.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-divider-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-mgb gdlr-core-divider-item-normal gdlr-core-center-align\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div id=\"map\" class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper \" data-skin=\"Blue Icon\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-content gdlr-core-js \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-container clearfix gdlr-core-container\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(59, 'day', 'Cairo Day Tour from Alexandria to visit Giza Pyramids & Grand  Egyptian Museum', 'Alexandria to Cairo', '1789315300_tour.jpeg', 185.00, 95.00, 90.00, 'Full Day', '7 am or 8am', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Cairo top attraction tour starts every day, Private Tour includes all Pick up &amp; drop off transfers from Alexandria port to Cairo, professional tour guide, All Taxes Services, Bottle of Water and All Transfers by Private A/C modern Vehicle, Tour excludes personal items, tipping, Mummies Room and any Optional Tours.</p>\r\n<p>there is possibility to enter one of the pyramids from Inside, visiting solar boat of king Cheops, riding camel around of Giza pyramids or ridding the quad bike at the wide desert or visiting the mummies room at the Egyptian museum or Felucca boat ride sailing on the Nile but all those excursions can be added on the middle of the tour as it requires additional fees .</p>', NULL, '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Lunch</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the Pyramids from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Comfortable shoes</li>\r\n<li>sun glasses</li>\r\n<li>sun block</li>\r\n<li>hat</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>our Egyptologist tour guide will be waiting inside your hotel in Alexandria, then you will Travel to CAIRO by Private Modern A/C mini Bus arrival to Cairo and Start your Day Tour Visiting<br><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Giza Pyramids and the Great Sphinx</span>, the most famous monuments of ancient world! These massive stone structures were built around 4,500 years ago on a rocky desert plateau close to the Nile and always amaze visitors. From there we move to have lunch at a local restaurant with the view of the Pyramids.</p>\r\n<p>Afternoon will move to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">the grand Egyptian Museum</span> which displays a rare collection of 5000 years of art. Over 250,000 genuine artifacts are presented, including an exhibit dedicated to Tutankhamen collection of treasure, gold, and jewelry which was enclosed in his tomb for over 3,500 years.<br>End your tour by a shopping stop at <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Khan el khalily Bazar</span> .<br>You cannot complete your visit to Cairo without a stop to Khan EL Khalili bazaar, one of the most famous and oldest bazaars in the Middle East.<br>Finally, your guide will take you back to Alexandria.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to the day tour as like:</strong><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/fascinating-cairo-dinner-cruise-on-nile/\">Cairo Dinner Cruise</a>.<br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/sound-and-light-show-at-giza-pyramids/\">Sound and Light Show at Giza Pyramids</a>.<br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/tour-to-wekalet-el-ghoury-for-tanoura-egyptian-heritage-dance-show/\">Al Tannoura Egyptian Heritage Show at Wekalet El Ghory</a> .</p>'),
(61, 'package', 'Egypt’s Highlights Tours 2 Days 1 Night: Giza & Cairo', 'Cairo', '1789436196_tour.jpeg', 225.00, 450.00, 225.00, '2 Days / 1 Night', '8:00AM', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item gdlr-core-item-pdb clearfix  gdlr-core-left-align gdlr-core-title-item-caption-bottom gdlr-core-item-pdlr\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title-wrap\">\r\n<h6 class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title gdlr-core-skin-title\">Tour Details</h6>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>Come with me on a life-time tour to the most impressive structures of the Pharaohs : the Great Pyramid , the Sphinx and the Step Pyramid. Tick another wonder off your bucket list and see the Great Pyramid &ndash; the only wonder of the ancient world still standing. Take a camel across the Sahara Desert and take the best panoramic pictures of ALL the pyramids, Private tour package includes 1 Nights hotel accommodation in Cairo on bed and breakfast basis, 1 full day tour in Giza visiting Giza pyramids, Sphinx, the step Pyramids of King Zoser at Saqqara &amp; Memphis, 1 full day tour in Cairo, All Transfers in Cairo, all your tours and excursions are with A/C car, the service of meet and assist at all your destinations, tour guide, and all taxes and services.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<div class=\"dual-lists\">\r\n<div>\r\n<ul class=\"styled-list exclude\">\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Entry Fees</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">accomodation</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Personal Items</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Tipping</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Unscheduled stops</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<h2 class=\"section-title\">&nbsp;</h2>\r\n</div>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Booking confirmation</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Comfortable shoes</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun glasses</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun block</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">hat</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<div id=\"itinerary\" class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-content gdlr-core-js \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-container clearfix gdlr-core-container\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb  gdlr-core-toggle-box-style-background-title hide gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-tab clearfix  gdlr-core-active\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-content-wrapper\">\r\n<h4 class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-title gdlr-core-js  gdlr-core-skin-e-background gdlr-core-skin-e-content\"><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><span class=\"gdlr-core-head\">Day 1-</span>Cairo Arrival -Giza Pyramids, Sphinx - Memphis - Sakkara Pyramids</span></h4>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>Arrival to Cairo airport, our professional tour Guide will meet you at the airport then from the airport Start your full day visiting <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Saqqara 27</strong></span> km southwest away from Cairo, where you can explore the first and oldest complete stone building complex known in history of the mankind which was built by Djoser during the third dynasty 2700 B c, Then Visit <strong><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Memphis</span></strong> , the ancient capital of Egypt, where the colossal statue of Ramses II and the great Alabaster Sphinx of Queen Hatshepsut . This City Dates back to 3100 B.C Then from there will go for lunch in a local restaurant with the view of the Giza pyramids (optional). After lunch go ahead to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Giza Pyramids and the Great Sphinx</strong></span>, the most famous monuments of ancient world! These massive stone structures were built around 4,500 years ago on a rocky desert plateau close to the Nile and always amaze visitors<br>At the end of the Tour you will be transferred back to your Hotel</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to the day tour as like:</strong><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/fascinating-cairo-dinner-cruise-on-nile/\">Cairo Dinner Cruise</a>.<br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/sound-and-light-show-at-giza-pyramids/\">Sound and Light Show at Giza Pyramids</a>.<br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/tour-to-wekalet-el-ghoury-for-tanoura-egyptian-heritage-dance-show/\">Al Tannoura Egyptian Heritage Show at Wekalet El Ghory</a>&nbsp;.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-tab clearfix \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-icon gdlr-core-js gdlr-core-skin-icon \">&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-content-wrapper\">\r\n<h4 class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-title gdlr-core-js  gdlr-core-skin-e-background gdlr-core-skin-e-content\"><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><span class=\"gdlr-core-head\">Day 2</span> - Grand Egyptian Museum - Citadel - Bazaar - Departure</span></h4>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div id=\"map\" class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper \" data-skin=\"Blue Icon\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-content gdlr-core-js \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-container clearfix gdlr-core-container\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item gdlr-core-item-pdb clearfix  gdlr-core-left-align gdlr-core-title-item-caption-bottom gdlr-core-item-pdlr\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title-wrap\">\r\n<p class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title gdlr-core-skin-title\">After Breakfast at your stay, our guide will pick you up to <strong><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">the Grand Egyptian Museum</span></strong> which displays a rare collection of 5000 years of art. Over 250,000 genuine artifacts are presented, including an exhibit dedicated to Tutankhamen collection of treasure, gold, and jewelry which was enclosed in his tomb for over 3,500 years.<br>After the museum will take a break for lunch at a local restaurant (optional) , then move ahead to visit to the outstanding <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Citadel of Saladin</strong></span>, a fortress built between 1176 and 1183 A.D. to protect Cairo from the Crusaders where you will visit <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>the mosque of Mohamed Ali</strong></span>, the founder of modern Egypt, and his mosque is a Turkish style mosque and called the Alabaster mosque. End your tour by a shopping stop at <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Khan el khalily Bazar</strong></span><br>You cannot complete your visit to Cairo without a stop to Khan EL Khalili bazaar, one of the most famous and oldest bazaars in the Middle East.<br>Finally at the end of the day we will transfer you back to Cairo international airport</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<div class=\"mapouter\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(62, 'transfer', 'Cairo or sphinx  Airport  private Transfers', 'Cairo Airport', '1789351070_tour.jpg', 25.00, 45.00, 25.00, 'Transfer', 'according to travellers dates', 'English, Arabic', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>We Provide&nbsp;<strong>Cairo or sphinx airport Transfers&nbsp;</strong>whether&nbsp;you want to book an transfer from Cairo airport to your hotel in Cairo or Vice Versa from your Hotel in Cairo or Giza to &nbsp;Cairo airport why you take a taxi from the airport while you can take &nbsp;a private transfer and almost with same cost . Thecheapest Pickup Transfers from Cairo airport to anywhere within Cairo or Giza.</p>\r\n<p>Book Online Your Pickup Transfer from Cairo airport and save your time, Private Always on time,Safe and Hassle free</p>\r\n<p><strong>Pick up from or to Cairo or sphinx airport to Cairo or Giza Hotels</strong></p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking driver</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Unscheduled stops</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>As Per Requested time you will be met by our Egypt travel square Representative in<strong> cairo or sphinx</strong> airport who will greet you with a sign shows your name on it then you will be transferred to your Hotel in Cairo or Giza</p>'),
(63, 'half', 'Giza pyramids by camel or horse (Photography & Highlights)', 'Cairo', '1789352521_tour.jpg', 50.00, 75.00, 50.00, '4 Hours', '9:00AM', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Half day tour for 4 hours starts every day upon request from 7:00 AM to: 5:00 PM Private tour includes all pickup and drop off transfers from guest stay in Cairo, professional Tour guide, Our Prices Includes All Taxes Services, all Transfers by modern Private Air Conditioned Car, Bottle of Water, tour excludes Personal Items, Tipping and any Optional Tours.</p>\r\n<p>There is possibility of entering any of the pyramids from inside, visiting solar boat of king cheops, riding camel around of Giza pyramids or ridding the quad bike at the wide desert but all those Excursion can be added on in the middle of the tour with your guide</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Unscheduled stops</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Our tour Starts With Pick you up from your stay in Cairo or Giza to be transferred to Giza Pyramids in a Private A-C Vehicle with the arrival to Giza Pyramids, you will get on the camel and will start your interesting Tour to Giza Pyramids by a very unique entrance to the desert that does not need you to move through the busy streets, Instead you will experience the virgin desert. You will ride between The Great Pyramids of Giza, The Sphinx and valley Temple it`s unusual test when visiting Giza Pyramids on Camel you feel like you are returning the time machine that will take you hundreds of years back and explore the ancient history and you will be guided by an expert tour guide who will explain all historical points that related to Giza Pyramids. After that you will be transferred back to your Hotel.</p>'),
(67, 'day', 'Aswan Day tour from Luxor City', 'Aswan / Luxor', '1789317100_tour.jpg', 195.00, 295.00, 195.00, '14 Hours', '7 :00am ', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Day tour approx. 14 Hours starts every day from 6:00 am to 5:00 pm, private tour includes Pick up services from your hotel in Luxor and return, all transfers by a private air-conditioned vehicle, Private English-speaking Egyptologist guide, lunch at a good quality restaurant, , Bottle of water and All service charges &amp; taxes, Tour excludes Any extras, Tipping and Any Optional Tour.</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Lunch</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item gdlr-core-item-pdb clearfix  gdlr-core-left-align gdlr-core-title-item-caption-bottom gdlr-core-item-pdlr\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title-wrap\">\r\n<h6 class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title gdlr-core-skin-title\">Itinerary</h6>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>Our expert guide At 6:00 am Pick you up from your Hotel or Nile Cruise in Luxor then you will be transferred by Private A/C Vehicle to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Edfu</strong></span> City where you visit<span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"> Temple of Horus in Edfu The Temple of Edfu</span> it&rsquo;s an ancient Egyptian temple located on the west bank of the Nile in the city of Edfu around an 1hr and half south of Luxor it was known in Greco-Roman times as Apollonopolis Magna, after the chief god Horus-Apollo.<br>It is one of the best preserved temples in Egypt. The temple, dedicated to the falcon god Horus, was built in the Ptolemaic period between 237 and 57 BCE. The inscriptions on its walls provide important information on language, myth and religion during the Greco-Roman period in ancient Egypt after you done your visit to Edfu Continue drive to Kom Ombo City where you you will visit the Temple of Kom Ombo it&rsquo;s an unusual double temple built during the Ptolemaic dynasty in the Egyptian town of <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Kom Ombo</strong></span>.<br>Some additions to it were later made during the Roman period. The building is unique because its &lsquo;double&rsquo; design meant that there were courts, halls, sanctuaries and rooms duplicated for two sets of gods.<br>The southern half of the temple was dedicated to<span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"> the crocodile god Sobek</span>, god of fertility and creator of the world with Hathor and Khonsu, then Continue drive towards Aswan Arrival Aswan and transfer you to a local restaurant for lunch included After Lunch you will be transferred to Continue your day tour to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Phila Temple</span> it is an island in Lake Nasser, Egypt.<br>It was formerly an island in the First Cataract of the Nile River and the previous site of an Ancient Egyptian temple complex in southern Egypt then End your day Tour By a visit to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">The High dam</span> that was constructed in 1961 by The President Nasr.<br>Around 06:00 pm Transfer you Back to your Hotel in Luxor or in Aswan if Our Customer intends to stay at Aswan instead of Returning back to Luxor.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>');
INSERT INTO `tours` (`id`, `type`, `title`, `location`, `hero_image`, `price`, `price_single`, `price_group_small`, `duration`, `timing`, `languages`, `availability`, `overview`, `includes_html`, `excludes_html`, `brings_html`, `itinerary`) VALUES
(68, 'day', 'Aswan highlight Full day Tour to Philae Temple, High Dam and Unfinished Obelisk', 'Aswan', '1789337325_tour.jpg', 75.00, 145.00, 75.00, '8 Hours', 'Hotel Pickup: 08:00 AM Hotel Return: 04:00 PM', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Private tour 8Hours Runs Daily at 8:00 am, includes Pick up service from your hotel in Aswan and return, Professional English-speaking tour guide, all transfers by a modern air-conditioned vehicle, Bottled water during your trip and Our Prices Includes All service charges &amp; taxes, Tour excludes Tipping, Optional activities and Personal expenses Visiting three of Aswan&rsquo;s most popular sites: the high Dam built between 1960 and 1970 &amp; protected Egypt from floods then to proceed to the unfinished Obelisk and finally enjoy the natural beauty of Philae Temple&rsquo;s island .</p>\r\n<p>There is possibility to ride horse carriage in the cornich st of Aswan and through the city or short felucca ride on the Nile River or the Nubian village but all those Excursion can be added on in the middle of tour with your guide.</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Lunch</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Unscheduled stops</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Our &nbsp;Expert tour guide At 8:00 am will pick you up from your hotel or Nile cruise or even from the airport in Aswan to enjoy a day tour in the amazing city of Aswan Start your tour by a visit to <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong>the High Dam,</strong></span> an engineering miracle built in 1960 protecting Egypt from annual floods from the Nile. Then proceed to visit <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong>the Unfinished Obelisk</strong></span> which shows the techniques used by the ancient Egyptians to cut obelisks, this obelisk belongs to Queen Hatshepsut, one of the rulers of the 18th Dynasty then Move to visit <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong>the majestic Philae Temple</strong></span> which was built in the honor of Goddess Isis the chief deity of the island. Later you will be transferred back to your hotel.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to the day tour as like:</strong><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/philae-temple-sound-and-light-show-aswan/\">Sound and Light Show at Philae Temple</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/aswan-city-tour-on-horse-carriage/\">Carriage ridding in Aswan</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/felucca-ride-on-the-nile-in-aswan/\">Short felucca ride in Aswan</a></p>'),
(69, 'day', 'Cairo City Tour to Egyptian Civilization  Museum, Citadel & Khan Khalily Bazaar', 'Cairo', '1789345469_tour.jpg', 75.00, 95.00, 75.00, '8 Hours', 'Hotel Pickup: 08:30 AM Hotel Return: 04:00 PM', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>In this day tour I will show you the Great artifacts in the Egyptian&nbsp; civilization Museum , I will help you to learn and understand more about art in ancient Egypt , we will explore the museum in a chronological order to trace the diverse history of Egypt and to enjoy the skills of the ancient Egyptian artists in a vey interesting way , then we go to the citadel of Saladin a great medieval architect , and we also will visit the alabaster mosque of Mohamed Ali , we will have time to take great pictures of Cairo from a panoramic View , Then we end the tour visiting the Old Church of saint sergious and Bakhous and visit the Old Synagogue<br>on travel in between sites Lunch and shopping stops can be arranged</p>\r\n<p>, such an indescribable feeling you will get, because today you will do Private tour includes all Pick up &amp; drop off transfers from Guest&prime;s location in Cairo or Giza, Expert Tour guide, (Bottle of Water) and All Transfers by Private modern A/C Vehicles,&nbsp; visiting ( the Egyptian museum Tour, Saladin fortress with Mohamed&nbsp; Ali mosque &amp; khan el khalily Bazaar)&nbsp; tour excludes personal items, tipping and Mummies Room.<br>________________________________________<br>There is possibility,</p>\r\n<p>Felucca ride on the Nile but all those Options can be added on in the middle of the tour with your Guide as it requires additional fees</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Unscheduled stops</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of thesites from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<div id=\"itinerary\" class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-content gdlr-core-js \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-container clearfix gdlr-core-container\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>After Breakfast at your stay, our guide will pick you up to <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">the Egyptian civilization Museum</span> which displays a rare collection of 5000 years of art. Over 250,000 genuine artifacts are presented, including an exhibit dedicated to Tutankhamen collection of treasure, gold, and jewelry which was enclosed in his tomb for over 3,500 years.<br>After the museum will take a break for lunch at a local restaurant (optional), then move ahead to visit to the outstanding <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Citadel of Saladin</span>, a fortress built between 1176 and 1183 A.D. to protect Cairo from the Crusaders where you will visit <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">the mosque of Mohamed Ali,</span> the founder of modern Egypt, and his mosque is a Turkish style mosque and called the Alabaster mosque, End your tour by a shopping stop at <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Khan el khalily Bazar</span><br>You cannot complete your visit to Cairo without a stop to Khan EL Khalili bazaar, one of the most famous and oldest bazaars in the Middle East.<br>Finally, we drive you back to your hotel in Cairo.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to the day tour as like:</strong><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/fascinating-cairo-dinner-cruise-on-nile/\">Cairo Dinner Cruise</a>.<br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/sound-and-light-show-at-giza-pyramids/\">Sound and Light Show at Giza Pyramids</a>.<br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/tour-to-wekalet-el-ghoury-for-tanoura-egyptian-heritage-dance-show/\">Al Tannoura Egyptian Heritage Show at Wekalet El Ghory</a>&nbsp;.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-divider-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-mgb gdlr-core-divider-item-normal gdlr-core-center-align\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div id=\"map\" class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper \" data-skin=\"Blue Icon\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-content gdlr-core-js \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-container clearfix gdlr-core-container\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item gdlr-core-item-pdb clearfix  gdlr-core-left-align gdlr-core-title-item-caption-bottom gdlr-core-item-pdlr\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title-wrap\">\r\n<h6 class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title gdlr-core-skin-title\">&nbsp;</h6>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<div class=\"mapouter\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(74, 'day', 'Luxor fantastic Day Tour to visit Dendera and Abydos temples from Luxor city', 'Luxor', '1789316915_tour.jpg', 95.00, 195.00, 95.00, '9Hours', '7:00 AM or 8:00 AM', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Dendera and Abydos tour approx. 10 Hours Runs daily from 7:00 am to 5:00 pm, private tour includes Pick up services from hotel in Luxor and return, all transfers by a private A/C vehicle, Private Egyptologist guide,Bottle of water, Tour excludes Any extras not mentioned in the program and Tipp</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Lunch</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Our professional tour Guide At 7:00 am will Pick you up from your Hotel or Nile Cruise in Luxor by Private A/C Vehicle to Abydos city Drive north from Luxor for a day to see two of the most complete temples in Egypt.<br>Arrival Abydos Start your day Tour discovering the ancient sites. First, visit Abydos Temple. Temple of Hathor at Dendara may be the best preserved in Egypt with full color still visible on its walls Temple around 135 km from Luxor, the ancient Egyptian believed of god (Lord of the underworld) to be buried there. The temple was built by King Seti I, and completed by King Ramsess II, known as temple of Seti I.<br>It is located in Abydos city about 420 km to the south of Cairo in Sohag Government, and 135 km from Luxor. The paintings of the Gods and Pharaohs on the walls of the Osiris Temple at Abydos are among the most beautifully preserved in Egypt. Then continue to Dendara to visit the Temple of Hathor, goddess of love and joy.<br>The temple is located in Dendara which is situated at the north of Luxor at the end of the Tour around 17:00 pm transfer back to the hotel in Luxor.</p>'),
(76, 'half', 'Sunrise or Sunset Camel ride tour at Giza Pyramids', 'Cairo', 'https://d3rr2gvhjw0wwy.cloudfront.net/uploads/activity_headers/234863/2000x2000-0-70-f65625f28a2a58eec273d0a4f30b8df9.jpg', 50.00, 65.00, 50.00, '2.5 Hours', 'any time before 6:00 pm', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>See the top attractions in an action-packed vacation, with an Egyptologist guide. Explore the spectacular Giza pyramids, the Great Sphinx Private Camels tour starts every day at any time from 6:00 am for sunrise tour and 5:30 pm for sunset tour, Private trip includes Ride Fees, Expert Tour guide, Snacks, All Taxes, Services and All Pickup &amp; drop off transfers from Customer stay in Cairo or Giza, Tour excludes Personal Items, Tipping, Visit to Giza Pyramids itself and any Optional Tours.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<div class=\"dual-lists\">\r\n<div>\r\n<ul class=\"styled-list exclude\">\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Entry Fees</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Personal Items</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Tipping</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Unscheduled stops</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<h2 class=\"section-title\">&nbsp;</h2>\r\n</div>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Booking confirmation</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Comfortable shoes</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun glasses</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun block</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">hat</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Our professional tour guide at 5:30 am or 5:00 Pm&nbsp;Pickup from your Hotel and transfer you to Giza area where Camel Stables located, then you will ride your Camel and enjoy your ride with our guide who will join you &nbsp;with the Camel man to make sure that you will be in safe hand then will start your interesting Tour to Giza Pyramids by a very unique entrance to the desert that does not need you to move through the busy streets, Instead you will experience the virgin desert. You will ride between The Great Pyramids of Giza,&nbsp;<strong>The Sphinx&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong>valley Temple</strong>&nbsp;it`s unusual test when visiting Giza Pyramids on Camel you feel like you are returning the time machine that will take you hundreds of years back and explore the ancient history and you will be guided by an expert tour guide who will explain all historical points that related to Giza Pyramids. After that you will be transferred&nbsp;back to your Hotel.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>'),
(78, 'day', 'Day Tour to Giza Pyramids, Memphis and Saqqara Pyramids', 'Cairo / Giza', '1789268911_tour.jpeg', 75.00, 95.00, 75.00, '7.5 Hours', '8:00AM', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>See the top attractions in an activity stuffed get-away, with an Egyptologist tour guide. Investigate the astounding Giza pyramids, the Great Sphinx, Sakkara and outside gallery</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Lunch</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the Pyramids from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Booking confirmation</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Comfortable shoes</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun glasses</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun block</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">hat</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Your professional Egyptologist will be waiting for you at your hotel lobby then will start your day visit Visiting <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>the Great Pyramids Of Giza &ndash; Cheops, Chephren and Mykerinos then Visit the Valley Temple </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">t</span></span>he Place where the Priests Mummified the dead group of lord Chephren proprietor of the second pyramid at Giza Platue Also it&rsquo;s a similar spot where you Can have a nearby glance at the Sphinx &ndash; The incredible watchman that stands by the immense burial service complex with its lion body and the head of ruler Chephren. Lunch is remembered for between visits at Local Restaurant Based on Full Meal for every Person except Beverages are excluded Then Continue your day visit to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Sakkara</strong></span>, found just 27 km southwest away from Cairo. Visit the <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Step Pyramid</span> (Built for ruler Zoser), it is viewed as a significant part during the time spent the pyramid advancement, which were produced using the straightforward mastaba to its commonly known structure. Then proceed with your day visit to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Memphis</strong></span>, the old capital of Egypt, where the goliath sculpture of Ramses II and the incomparable Alabaster Sphinx are. This City Dates back to 3100 B.C, An Optional shopping visit at the conventional markets where you can buy a scope of customary keepsakes, for example, scent oils, papyrus, hieroglyphics in various materials and so on then back to your hotel</p>'),
(81, 'half', 'Cairo Shopping Tour to Old  Market', 'Cairo', '1789270960_tour.jpeg', 35.00, 65.00, 35.00, '5 Hours', 'any time before 10:00 pm', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>The Khan El-Khalili is one of the most famous and oldest bazaars in the Middle East, All visitors can safely enjoy walking through the narrow streets of Khan El-Khalili. We strongly recommend visiting this vivid bazaar, but keep in mind that in open traditional markets, the prices are not set in stone. You always want to remember to bargain for the best price, all vendors will expect this and it can be pretty fun! The Khan El-Khalili Bazaar is a place where art and commerce come together to enjoy a unique and, harmonious experience.</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>our guide will pick you up to t<span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>he Khan el khalily Bazar</strong></span><br>You cannot complete your visit to Cairo without a stop to Khan EL Khalili bazaar, one of the most famous and oldest bazaars in the Middle East.<br>Finally, we drive you back to your hotel in Cairo.</p>'),
(84, 'day', 'Day Tour to Kom Ombo and Edfu temples from Aswan', 'Aswan', '1789337689_tour.jpeg', 9000.00, 190.00, 9000.00, '8 Hours', 'Hotel Pickup: 06:00 AM Hotel Return: 07:00 PM  ', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Day tour approx. 8 Hours starts every day from 7:00 am to 3:00 pm, private tour includes Pick up services from your hotel in Aswan and return, all transfers by a private air-conditioned vehicle, Private English-speaking Egyptologist guide, lunch at a good quality restaurant, Bottle of water and All service charges &amp; taxes, Tour excludes Any extras, Tipping and Any Optional Tour.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Lunch</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Unscheduled stops</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Our Egypt travel square tour guide At 7:00 am Pick you up from your Hotel or Nile Cruise in Aswan then you will be transferred by Private A/C Vehicle to Kom Ombo City where you you will visit <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong>the Temple of Kom Ombo</strong></span> it&rsquo;s an unusual double temple built during the Ptolemaic dynasty in the Egyptian town of Kom Ombo.<br>Some additions to it were later made during the Roman period. The building is unique because its &lsquo;double&rsquo; design meant that there were courts, halls, sanctuaries and rooms duplicated for two sets of gods.<br>The southern half of the temple was dedicated to the crocodile god Sobek, god of fertility and creator of the world with Hathor and Khonsu, then Continue drive towards Luxor to Edfu City where you visit Temple of Horus in Edfu <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong>The Temple of Edfu</strong></span> it&rsquo;s an ancient Egyptian temple located on the west bank of the Nile in the city of Edfu around an 1hr north of Aswan it was known in Greco-Roman times as Apollonopolis Magna, after the chief god Horus-Apollo.<br>It is one of the best preserved temples in Egypt. The temple, dedicated to the falcon god Horus, was built in the Ptolemaic period between 237 and 57 BCE. The inscriptions on its walls provide important information on language, myth and religion during the Greco-Roman period in ancient Egypt after you done your visit to Edfu Around 0400 pm Transfer you Back to your Hotel in Aswan if Our Customer intends to stay at Luxor instead of Returning back to Aswan.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to the day tour as like:</strong><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/philae-temple-sound-and-light-show-aswan/\">Sound and Light Show at Philae Temple</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/aswan-city-tour-on-horse-carriage/\">Carriage ridding in Aswan</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/felucca-ride-on-the-nile-in-aswan/\">Short felucca ride in Aswan</a></p>'),
(90, 'day', 'Fayoum Oasis Safari Day tour from Cairo by Car', 'Fayoum', '1789269729_tour.jpg', 150.00, 295.00, 150.00, '11 Hours', '7 am', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Fayoum Oasis tour starts every day from 7:00 am, Private tour includes all pick up &amp; drop off from Guest stay in Cairo, Transfer by private, air-conditioned Vehicle to Oasis and back, private 4WD Jeep tour in the desert, with a Professional tour guide, Bedouin driver.</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">lunch</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Booking confirmation</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Comfortable shoes</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun glasses</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun block</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">hat</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Our professional tour Guide will pick you up from your hotel in&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.memphistours.com/Egypt/Egypt-Wikis/Egypt-Destinations/wiki/Cairo\">Cairo</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;or Giza to enjoy&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.memphistours.com/Egypt/Egypt-Wikis/oases-and-the-western-desert/wiki/EL-Fayoum\">El Fayoum</a>&nbsp;Oasis famous sites.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.memphistours.com/Egypt/Egypt-Wikis/oases-and-the-western-desert/wiki/EL-Fayoum\">Fayoum</a>&nbsp;is about 95 km from Cairo. We will start our tour by 4DW Jeep &nbsp;to Wadi Hitan Protected Area (Valley of the Whales), about 95 km far from Fayoum. Valley of the Whales is located in the Protected Area of&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.memphistours.com/Egypt/WikiTravel/the-western-desert-and-oases/wiki/Wadi-Al-Rayan\">Wadi El Rayan</a>&nbsp;and it was designated by UNISCO as a world Heritage Site in recognition of the 40 million year &ndash;old whale skeletons found there. &nbsp;On the way to&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.memphistours.com/Egypt/WikiTravel/the-western-desert-and-oases/wiki/Wadi-Al-Rayan\">Wadi El Rayan</a>&nbsp;Water Falls, you will enjoy the beautiful view of the sahara&nbsp; sand dunes and you can do s and boarding there then &nbsp;we will visit Mudawara Mountain. Then into Wadi Al Ryan Water Falls. Wadi El Rayan is a natural depression located in the western desert, Wadi Rayan consists of two lakes connected by Egypt&rsquo;s only waterfalls, formed in 1970 by an overflow of drainage water from the farmlands in&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.memphistours.com/Egypt/Egypt-Wikis/oases-and-the-western-desert/wiki/EL-Fayoum\">Fayoum</a>, After that transfer back to&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.memphistours.com/Egypt/Egypt-Wikis/Egypt-Destinations/wiki/Cairo\">Cairo.</a><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;</strong></p>'),
(91, 'day', 'Local Day Tour To Giza Pyramids, Saladin Citadel & Old cairo', 'Cairo', 'https://media.tacdn.com/media/attractions-splice-spp-674x446/0f/27/64/69.jpg', 80.00, 170.00, 80.00, '8 Hours', '8:00AM', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>See the top attractions in an action-packed vacation, Private day Tour Includes All Pick Up &amp; Drop Off from your stay in Cairo or in Giza,&nbsp; Expert Tour Guide, All Taxes Services, (Bottle of Water) And All Transfers by Private modern A/C Vehicles. Explore the spectacular Giza pyramids, the Great Sphinx. Get awestruck by Old Cairo, and Saladin fortress with Mohamed Ali mosque.</p>\r\n<p>.</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Entry Fees</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Personal Items</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Tipping</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Unscheduled stops</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Booking confirmation</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Comfortable shoes</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun glasses</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun block</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">hat</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item gdlr-core-item-pdb clearfix  gdlr-core-left-align gdlr-core-title-item-caption-bottom gdlr-core-item-pdlr\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title-wrap\">\r\n<h6 class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title gdlr-core-skin-title\">Itinerary</h6>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>Our tour starts at 8:00 am Pick you up from&nbsp; your stay in Cairo By our guide to Start your full day tour by visiting to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Giza Pyramids and the Great Sphinx</strong></span>, the most famous monuments of ancient world! These massive stone structures were built around 4,500 years ago on a rocky desert plateau close to the Nile and always amaze visitors then move to visit the outstanding <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Citadel of Saladin,</strong></span> a fortress built between 1176 and 1183 A.D.</p>\r\n<p>to protect Cairo from the Crusaders where you will visit<span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong> the mosque of Mohamed Ali</strong></span>, the founder of modern Egypt, and his mosque is a Turkish style mosque and called the Alabaster mosque then stop for lunch in one of the local Restaurants(optional), After that our guide will pick you up to the<span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\"><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;visit </span><span style=\"color: #cc0000;\">Old Cairo,</span> home to some of the oldest churches in Egypt</span>,During the day, you will also have the chance to visit a Papyrus Museum to see how the famous paper is made, After that back to your hotel .</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>');
INSERT INTO `tours` (`id`, `type`, `title`, `location`, `hero_image`, `price`, `price_single`, `price_group_small`, `duration`, `timing`, `languages`, `availability`, `overview`, `includes_html`, `excludes_html`, `brings_html`, `itinerary`) VALUES
(93, 'day', 'Luxor Day Tour to visit the magnificent temples of Edfu and Kom Ombo from Luxor City', 'Luxor', '1789272019_tour.jpeg', 105.00, 210.00, 105.00, '10 Hours', '7 am or 8am', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item gdlr-core-item-pdb clearfix  gdlr-core-left-align gdlr-core-title-item-caption-bottom gdlr-core-item-pdlr\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title-wrap\">\r\n<h6 class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title gdlr-core-skin-title\">Tour Details</h6>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>Day tour approx. 10 Hours starts every day from 6:00 am to 5:00 pm, private tour includes Pick up services from your hotel in Luxor and return, all transfers by a private air-conditioned vehicle, Private English-speaking Egyptologist guide, lunch at a good quality restaurant, Bottle of water and All service charges &amp; taxes, Tour excludes Any extras, Tipping and Any Optional Tour.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Booking confirmation</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Comfortable shoes</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun glasses</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun block</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">hat</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Our Egypt travel square tour guide At 6:00 am Pick you up from your Hotel or Nile Cruise in Luxor then you will be transferred by Private A/C Vehicle to Edfu City where you visit Temple of Horus in Edfu The Temple of Edfu it&rsquo;s an ancient Egyptian temple located on the west bank of the Nile in the city of Edfu around an 1hr and half south of Luxor it was known in Greco-Roman times as Apollonopolis Magna, after the chief god Horus-Apollo.</p>\r\n<p>It is one of the best preserved temples in Egypt. The temple, dedicated to the falcon god Horus, was built in the Ptolemaic period between 237 and 57 BCE. The inscriptions on its walls provide important information on language, myth and religion during the Greco-Roman period in ancient Egypt after you done your visit to Edfu Continue drive to Kom Ombo City where you you will visit&nbsp;the Temple of Kom Ombo&nbsp;it&rsquo;s an unusual double temple built during the Ptolemaic dynasty in the Egyptian town of Kom Ombo.</p>\r\n<p>Some additions to it were later made during the Roman period. The building is unique because its &lsquo;double&rsquo; design meant that there were courts, halls, sanctuaries and rooms duplicated for two sets of gods.</p>\r\n<p>The southern half of the temple was dedicated to the crocodile god Sobek, god of fertility and creator of the world with Hathor and Khonsu, then Continue drive towards Aswan Arrival Aswan and transfer you to a local restaurant for lunch included After</p>\r\n<p>Around 0400 pm Transfer you Back to your Hotel in Luxor or in Aswan if Our Customer intends to stay at Aswan instead of Returning back to Luxor</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to the day tour as like:</strong><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/sound-and-light-show-at-karnak-temple-in-luxor/\">Sound and Light Show at Karnak Temple</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/luxor-city-tour-on-horse-carriage/\">Luxor City tour on Horse Carriage&nbsp;</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/felucca-ride-on-the-nile-in-luxor/\">Short felucca ride on the Nile River</a></p>'),
(96, 'half', 'Grand Egyptian Museum in Half Day Tour', 'Cairo', '1789271347_tour.jpeg', 55.00, 75.00, 55.00, '4 Hours', 'any time before 2:00 pm', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Half day tour for 4 hours starts every day upon request from 9 am till 5 pm except Sunday&nbsp; and Thursday till 9 pm&nbsp;&nbsp; , Private tour includes all pickup and drop off transfers from guest stay in Cairo, professional Tour guide, Our Prices Includes All Taxes Services, all Transfers by modern Private Air Conditioned Car, Bottle of Water, tour excludes Personal Items, Tipping and any Optional Tours.</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Lunch</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as&nbsp; Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Booking confirmation</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Comfortable shoes</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun glasses</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun block</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">hat</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Our professional tour guide will pick you up from your stay in Cairo or Giza to the Grand Egyptian Museum which displays a rare collection of 5000 years of art. Over 250,000 genuine artifacts are presented, including an exhibit dedicated to Tutankhamen collection of treasure, gold, and jewelry which was enclosed in his tomb for over 3,500 years. after that you will be transferred back to your Hotel.</p>'),
(97, 'day', 'Day Tour to Islamic and Christian Cairo', 'Cairo', '1789271609_tour.jpg', 65.00, 95.00, 65.00, '8 Hours', 'any time before mid day', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Interesting Tour like 8 hours starts every day from 7:00 am to 4:00 pm, private tour includes Pick up from your hotel and return, all transfers by a private A/C vehicle, Private guide, Entrance fees, , S (Bottle of water) and All service charges &amp; taxes, Tour excludes Any extras, Tipping</p>\r\n<p>There is possibility of entering any of the Coptic Museum or the Islamic Museum or Felucca boat ride sailing on the Nile But this can be added in the middle of the tour.</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Lunch</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as&nbsp; Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Our tour starts at 9:00 am Pickup from stay in Cairo By Egypt travel square guide to Start your full day tour by visiting <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Old Cairo</strong></span> that known as <strong>Christian Cairo</strong> or <strong>Coptic Cairo</strong> whichis the home of <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Cairo&rsquo;s Coptic Christian Orthodox community</span> where we visit the incredible <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Hanging Church</span>, In Arabic, Kineeset al-Muallaqa. The Hanging Church, built in 690, in the remains of the two southern towers of the Roman fortress 0f Babilon and its nave is suspended over a passageway.</p>\r\n<p>Then move to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">St. Sergius churchis</span> one of the oldest churches in Cairo, built in the 4th century A D which became very famous because it wasconstructed upon the crypt of the Holy Family where they stayed for three weeks during their flight here in Egypt, after that the old <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">jewish synagogue &ndash; Ben Ezra Synagogue</span>.<br>Lunch is in between visits at Local Restaurant then we will go head to see the Islamic Cairo.</p>\r\n<p>Egypt has an incredible art and architectural heritage that has lasted for hundreds years, beginning with the building of the 1st Islamic Mosque in Egypt and Africa Continent Which is Amr Ibn Alas Mosque in 642 A d . Cairo is full of medieval masterpieces that reflect the status of Egypt as the center of several significant Islamic empires<br>Islamic Cairo is the area of the city which holds the most, the greatest and the most famous Islamic monuments. Many of these were built by the Fatimid Rulers who founded the city Cairo Afterthe 1st Islamic capital Al Fustat or Old Cairo).</p>\r\n<p>Not like Islamic quarters in other cities, people, often quite poor, continue to live by historic monuments and mosques. A huge center of worship, trade, shopping and commuting .</p>\r\n<p>After Amr ibn Alas mosque we will move to visit the outstanding Citadel of Saladin, a fortress built between 1176 and 1183 A.D. to protect Cairo from the Crusaders where you will visit the mosque of Mohamed Ali, the founder of modern Egypt, and his mosque is a Turkish style mosque and called the Alabaster mosque, then Followed by a visit to the Most and vast mosques in Cairo which is El Sultan Hassan Mosque that also known as `Madrasa El Sultan Hassan` that was built by Sultan Hassan in 1356 A.D The Mosque-Madrassa of Sultan Hassan is located near The Citadel in Cairo.</p>\r\n<p>Its construction started in 1356 Ad<br>This mosque was considered remarkable for its fantastic size and innovative architectural components. Commissioned by a sultan The mosque was built to include schools for all four of the Sunni schools of thought: Shafi&rsquo;i, Maliki, Hanafi and Hanbali.<br>Then Followed by another big famous Mosque which is Al-Rifa&rsquo;i Mosque The Mosque is located opposite the Mosque and Madrassa of Sultan Hassan,<br>At the end of the Tour, you will be transferred back to your Hotel</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>'),
(98, 'transfer', 'Pick up from or to Luxor airport to Luxor Hotels', 'Luxor', '1789271492_tour.jpg', 25.00, 45.00, 25.00, 'Flexible', 'according to travellers dates', 'English, Arabic', 'according to travellers dates', '<p>Available upon request for both Arrival rDeparture from Luxor airport available 24/7.</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking driver</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the Sites from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>As Per Requested time You will be met by our Egypt travel square Representative in Luxor airport who will greet you with a sign shows your name on it then you will be transferred to your Hotel in Luxor,Budget and Cheap airport Transfers Only with Egypt travel square, Also available from Your Hotel or Nile Cruise in Luxor to Luxor airport</p>'),
(100, 'package', 'Egypt’s Adventure 6 Days 5 Nights Tours to Cairo & White Desert', 'Cairo / Bahariya', '1789271908_tour.jpg', 650.00, 0.00, 0.00, '6 Days / 5 Nights', 'according to travellers dates', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'according to travellers dates', '', NULL, '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '', ''),
(103, 'package', 'Egypt Package 8 DAYS 7 NIGHTS CAIRO, NILE CRUISE ASWAN, LUXOR AND ABU SIMBEL', 'Cairo / Aswan / Luxor', '1789271065_tour.jpg', 1950.00, 2550.00, 1950.00, '8 Days / 7 Nights', ' mid day', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'according to cruise dates Pickup: 08:00 AM Hotel Return: 04:30 PM', '<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item gdlr-core-item-pdb clearfix  gdlr-core-left-align gdlr-core-title-item-caption-bottom gdlr-core-item-pdlr\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title-wrap\">\r\n<h6 class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title gdlr-core-skin-title\">Tour Details</h6>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>Here&rsquo;s your best chance to see the best heritage of Egypt and learn how the Egyptians make history.</p>\r\n<p>Take a fantastic Private tour package includes 3 Nights hotel accommodation in Cairo on bed and breakfast basis, 3 Nights Nile cruise from Aswan to Luxor full board</p>\r\n<p>1 full day tour in Giza visiting Giza pyramids, Sphinx, the step Pyramids of King Zoser at Saqqara &amp; Memphis.</p>\r\n<p>full day tour in Cairo.</p>\r\n<p>All Transfers in Cairo.</p>\r\n<p>all your tours and excursions are with A/C car.</p>\r\n<p>the service of meet and assist at all your destinations, tour guide, and all taxes and services.</p>\r\n<p>there is possibility to enter one of the pyramids from Inside, visiting solar boat of king Cheops, riding camel around of Giza pyramids or ridding the quad bike at the wide desert or visiting the mummies room at the Egyptian&nbsp;museum or&nbsp;Felucca boat ride sailing on the Nile but all those excursions can be added on the middle of the tour as it requires additional fees&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<h4 class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-title gdlr-core-js  gdlr-core-skin-e-background gdlr-core-skin-e-content\"><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><span class=\"gdlr-core-head\">Day 1-</span>Cairo Arrival</span></h4>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>Arrival at Cairo airport. Our airport representative will be there holding a sign of your name to meet and assist you through the airport formalities. Then transfer to your hotel.</p>\r\n<h4 class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-title gdlr-core-js  gdlr-core-skin-e-background gdlr-core-skin-e-content\"><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><span class=\"gdlr-core-head\">Day 2-</span> Pyramids of Giza &ndash; Saqqara -Memphis</span></h4>\r\n<p>our professional tour Guide will meet you at the airport then from the airport Start your full day visiting <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong>Saqqara</strong></span>27 km southwest away from Cairo, where you can explore the first and oldest complete stone building complex known in history of the mankind which was built by Djoser during the third dynasty 2700 B c. times. Then move to the most Interesting highlights of Saqqara after the pyramids of Djoser, Which is<strong> <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Unas pyramid, Teti pyramid</span></strong>. And the daily life inscriptions in the outstanding old kingdom high official tombs such as Mereruka, Kagemni, Ptah-hotep family and Mehu. The new kingdom tombs such as Horemhep, Maya, Tia and Merynieth. And the unique Serapeum of the sacred bull Apis .Then Visit<span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong> Memphis </strong></span>, the ancient capital of Egypt, where the colossal statue of Ramses II and the great Alabaster Sphinx 0f Queen Hatshepsut . This City Dates back to 3100 B.C Then from there will go for lunch in a local restaurant with the view of the Giza pyramids. After lunch go ahead to <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong>Giza Pyramids</strong></span> and the Great Sphinx, the most famous monuments of ancient world! These massive stone structures were built around 4,500 years ago on a rocky desert plateau close to the Nile and always amaze visitors<br>At the end of the Tour you will be transferred back to your Hotel.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to the day tour as like:</strong><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/fascinating-cairo-dinner-cruise-on-nile/\">Cairo Dinner Cruise</a>.<br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/sound-and-light-show-at-giza-pyramids/\">Sound and Light Show at Giza Pyramids</a>.<br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/tour-to-wekalet-el-ghoury-for-tanoura-egyptian-heritage-dance-show/\">Al Tannoura Egyptian Heritage Show at Wekalet El Ghory</a> .</p>\r\n<h4 class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-title gdlr-core-js  gdlr-core-skin-e-background gdlr-core-skin-e-content\"><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><span class=\"gdlr-core-head\">Day 3-</span>Aswan</span></h4>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>our representative At 4:00 am will pick you up from your hotel to Cairo airport to fly to <strong><span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Aswan </span></strong>to enjoy a day tour in the amazing city of Aswan Start your tour by a visit to the <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">High Dam,</span> an engineering miracle built in 1960 protecting Egypt from annual floods from the Nile, Then transfer to the Cruise. Boarding before lunch, Embarkation. Lunch on board. Then Move to visit the majestic <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Philae Temple </span>which was built in the honor of Goddess Isis the chief deity of the island. <strong>Dinner on board, overnight in Aswan.</strong></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong>Meals: Full Board</strong></span></p>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-tab clearfix gdlr-core-active\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-content-wrapper\">\r\n<h4 class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-title gdlr-core-js  gdlr-core-skin-e-background gdlr-core-skin-e-content\"><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><span class=\"gdlr-core-head\">Day 4- </span>Aswan - Abu Simbel</span></h4>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>early morning transfer you to <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong>Abu Simbel Temple </strong></span>where<br>The Colossal Temple of Abu Simbel built by Ramses II (XIX century, Dynasty) and lately saved from the flood of the waters of the Nile amid the glories of ancient Egyptian monuments. The temples were built on a cliff of sandstone, and the representation of the deities to which each one dedicated himself is carved in its enormous fa&ccedil;ade. Nearby, there is also the small temple of the king&rsquo;s favorite wife (Nefertari), dedicated to the goddess Hathor. Then transfer to the cruise<br>Return to Nile Cruise then start to sail to <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">KomOmbo.</span> Afternoon Visit the temple shared by the two gods Sobek and Horusthen Sail to Edfu. <strong>Dinner on board. Overnight in Edfu.</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Meals: Full Board</strong></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-tab clearfix \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-icon gdlr-core-js gdlr-core-skin-icon \">\r\n<h4 class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-title gdlr-core-js  gdlr-core-skin-e-background gdlr-core-skin-e-content\"><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><span class=\"gdlr-core-head\">Day 5- </span>kom ombo - Edfu</span></h4>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>Breakfast on board. Then Visit<span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"> The Temple of Horus in Edfu</span>. Cross the lock. Sail to Luxor. Full Day Tour to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>The East Bank </strong></span>Visiting<span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"> Karnak</span> <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Temple</span>, the greatest example of worship in the history, dedicated to the main triad of Luxor (God Amon, his wife Mut and their son Khonsu).<br>Finish your day tour by visiting the<span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"> Temple Of Luxor</span>, it was built by Amenhotep III in 18th Dynasty in the New Kingdom and it was completed by Ramses&rsquo; II during the 19th Dynasty Dinner on board &amp; Galabya party. Overnight in Luxor</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Overnight in Luxor.</span></p>\r\n<p><strong>Meals: Full Board</strong></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-content-wrapper\">\r\n<h4 class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-title gdlr-core-js  gdlr-core-skin-e-background gdlr-core-skin-e-content\"><span class=\"gdlr-core-head\" style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Day 6- Luxor East &amp; west bank - Cairo</span></h4>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>Breakfast on board then check out .then move to <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">the West Bank</span> to visit <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Valley of the Kings, the Temple of Hatshepsut</span> and the Colossi of Memnon. The Excursion to the Valley of Kings; visit the tombs of various Dynasties, The Temple of Deir El Bahari. On the return journey stop at <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">the Colossi of Memnon</span> which are two gigantic sitting statues representing Amenophis III facing the Nile. And visit the Temple of Queen Hatshepsut. Transfer to the airport. Departure by a plane to <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Cairo</span>. Arrival, meet and assist by our representative. Transfer to your hotel. <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong>Overnight in Cairo.</strong></span></p>\r\n<p><strong>Meals: Breakfast</strong></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-content\">\r\n<h4 class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-title gdlr-core-js  gdlr-core-skin-e-background gdlr-core-skin-e-content\"><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><span class=\"gdlr-core-head\">Day 7- Grand </span>Egyptian museum--Coptic Cairo and Islamic Cairo</span></h4>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>visit <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">the Grand Egyptian Museum</span> which displays a rare collection of 5000 years of art. Over 250,000 genuine artifacts are presented, including an exhibit dedicated to Tutankhamen collection of treasure, gold, and jewelry which was enclosed in his tomb for over 3,500 years.<br>After the museum will take a break for lunch at a local restaurant, then move ahead to visit to the outstanding <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Citadel of Saladin</span>, a fortress built between 1176 and 1183 A.D. to protect Cairo from the Crusaders where you will visit the mosque of Mohamed Ali, the founder of modern Egypt, and his mosque is a Turkish style mosque and called the Alabaster mosque.End your tour by a shopping stop at<span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"> Khan el khalily Bazar</span><br>You cannot complete your visit to Cairo without a stop to Khan EL Khalili bazaar, one of the most famous and oldest bazaars in the Middle East.<br>Finally at the end of the day we will transfer you to your hotel in Cairo.</p>\r\n<h4 class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-title gdlr-core-js  gdlr-core-skin-e-background gdlr-core-skin-e-content\"><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><span class=\"gdlr-core-head\">Day 8-</span>Final Departure</span></h4>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>Breakfast at the hotel and transfer to the <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Cairo International Airport</span> for your final departure.<br>Meals: Breakfast.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(104, 'half', 'Old Egyptian Museum in Half Day ', 'Cairo', '1789270822_tour.jpg', 55.00, 75.00, 55.00, '4 Hours', 'any time before 3:00 pm', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Half day tour for 4 hours starts every day upon request from 9 am till 5 pm except Sunday&nbsp; and Thursday till 9 pm&nbsp;&nbsp; , Private tour includes all pickup and drop off transfers from guest stay in Cairo, professional Tour guide, Our Prices Includes All Taxes Services, all Transfers by modern Private Air Conditioned Car, Bottle of Water, tour excludes Personal Items, Tipping and any Optional Tours.</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">lunch</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Booking confirmation</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Comfortable shoes</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun glasses</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">sun block</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">hat</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Our professional tour guide will pick you up from your stay in Cairo or Giza to the Egyptian Museum which displays a rare collection of 5000 years of art. Over 250,000 genuine artifacts are presented, including an exhibit dedicated to Tutankhamen collection of treasure, gold, and jewelry which was enclosed in his tomb for over 3,500 years. after that you will be transferred back to your Hotel.</p>'),
(105, 'day', 'Fabulous Safari DAY TRIP TO BAHARIYA OASIS, BLACK AND WHITE DESERT FROM CAIRO', 'Bahariya Oasis', '1789270722_tour.jpg', 180.00, 320.00, 180.00, 'Full Day', '7:00 am', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Unforgettable Bahariya&nbsp; Oasis Day tour starts every day from 6:00 am to 11:00 pm, Private tour includes all pick up &amp; drop off from Guest stay in Cairo, Transfer by private, air-conditioned Vehicle to Oasis and back, Private 4WD Jeep tour in the desert, with a Professional tour guide, Bedouin Breakfast and lunch in the Desert and dinner.</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Tipping</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>Early morning our professional tour guide&nbsp;<strong>At 06:00</strong>&nbsp;will pick you up from your stay in&nbsp;Cairo or Giza and transfer you in a modern private A/C &nbsp;vehicle&nbsp;to&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Bahariya Oasis</strong></span>&nbsp;about 380 km south&nbsp;west of &nbsp;Giza, the driving takes about 5hours, with the arrival to&nbsp;Baharaia Oasis capital&nbsp;<strong>Al Bawity</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;will change car to 4WD Jeep then move 40 km through the desert to see the sand dunes, then the<strong>&nbsp;black desert.</strong></p>\r\n<p>Then lunch will be served at one of the Oasis hot springs&nbsp; called el Hez where you can swim relax before or after lunch</p>\r\n<p>Then direct drive for 92 km to&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>crystal Mountains &amp; al &nbsp;Agbatat Mountains</strong>&nbsp; then move to<strong>&nbsp;the white desert</strong>&nbsp;which Contains collection&nbsp; of wonderful white amazing rocks take the shape of so forms like; mushrooms, chicken &amp; rabbit. Drive back to Cairo</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-divider-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-mgb gdlr-core-divider-item-normal gdlr-core-center-align\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>');
INSERT INTO `tours` (`id`, `type`, `title`, `location`, `hero_image`, `price`, `price_single`, `price_group_small`, `duration`, `timing`, `languages`, `availability`, `overview`, `includes_html`, `excludes_html`, `brings_html`, `itinerary`) VALUES
(107, 'half', 'Felucca Ride on the Nile in Aswan', 'Aswan', '1789270542_tour.jpg', 45.00, 65.00, 45.00, '2 Hours', 'any time before 7:00 pm', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Private Tour for 2 Hours Runs Daily as Per Request time, Private trip includes Expert Tour guide, All Taxes &amp; Services and All Pickup and drop off transfers, Bottle of water for each during your tour, tour excludes any extras and Tipping.</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">lunch</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Your Local guide will pick you up from your hotel (Reception Area), and transfer to the Nile side, where your Felucca is waiting for you journey. Board your Felucca Nile Sailing and relax on the Soft cushions. Experience the peace and tranquility of the Nile water around Elephantine Island and to visit the Botanical Gardens, which is rich of its plants that were imported from all over the world In the year of 1899 Lord Kitchener used this Island to be a place where his campaign can rest, and call it the Lord&rsquo;s house, the children playing in the water, the camels and donkeys, the farmers going about their work in the same ways they have done for centuries, and admire the water buffalo and a wide variety of birds,</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Watch the sun sets slowly over Aswan City, take in the scenes of life around you as you sail along the Nile, back to the Nile side and then transfer to your hotel in Aswan.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to the day tour as like:</strong><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/philae-temple-sound-and-light-show-aswan/\">Sound and Light Show at Philae Temple</a></p>'),
(108, 'half', 'Felucca Ride on the Nile in Luxor', 'Luxor', '1789270573_tour.jpg', 45.00, 65.00, 45.00, '2 Hours', 'any time before 7:00 pm', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Tour for 2 Hours Runs every day at any Time from 4:00 pm, Private trip includes Expert Tour guide, All Taxes &amp; Services and All Pickup and drop off transfers, Bottle of water for each during your tour,tour excludes any extras and Tipping.</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">1-</span><span style=\"font-size: 7.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">2-</span><span style=\"font-size: 7.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">3-</span><span style=\"font-size: 7.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">All Transfers as mentioned.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">4- bottle of water for each person</span></p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">lunch</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Your Local guide will pick you up from your hotel (Reception Area), and transfer to the Nile side, where your Felucca is waiting for you journey. Board your Felucca Nile Sailing and relax on the Soft cushions. Experience the peace and tranquility of the Nile water that has been the lifeblood of Egypt since Pharaonic times. Enjoy a cool drink as you gently glide down the river. Watch the real Egyptian life pass by and enjoy the fantastic scenes that have not changed in millennia, the children playing in the water, the camels and donkeys, the farmers going about their work in the same ways they have done for centuries, and admire the water buffalo and a wide variety of birds.</p>\r\n<p>Watch the sun sets slowly over Luxor West Bank, take in the scenes of life around you as you sail along the Nile, back to the Nile side and then transfer to your hotel in Luxor.</p>'),
(109, 'half', 'Glass bottom boat in Sharm El Sheikh', 'Sharm El Sheikh', '1789270377_tour.jpg', 75.00, 95.00, 75.00, '4 Hours', '9;00AM', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'according to boat dates', '<p>4 Hours Runs Every Day, Private Trip includes, pick up service from your Hotel in Sharmand return, Professional English-speaking tour guide, bottle of water, Entry fees,all transfers by a modern air conditioned vehicle and All service charges &amp; taxes, Tour excludes Optional activities, tipping and Personal expenses</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Unscheduled stops</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Pick up from hotel in the morning by our representative,then drive for 20 minutes to the Glass Boat dock, join the boat, snorkeling<br>Enjoy the view of different Reefs, Corals &amp; Colored fish, so this is the life under water.</p>\r\n<p>, back to the dock and drive back to the hotel.</p>'),
(110, 'day', ' Alexandria Highlight Day Tour  from Cairo', 'Alexandria', '1789270138_tour.jpg', 85.00, 165.00, 85.00, 'Full Day', '7 am or 8am', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Private Full day tour starts Every day from 7 am to 4 pm includes all Pickup and drop off transfers from your Hotel in Alexandria, Professional English-speaking tour guide, all transfers by a modern A/C vehicle, Bottle water during your trip, all service charges &amp; taxes, Tour excludes Personal Items, Tipping and Optional activities.</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">lunch</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<div id=\"itinerary\" class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-content gdlr-core-js \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-container clearfix gdlr-core-container\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>7:00 am our Professional tour guide will pick you up from your stay in either Cairo or Giza then transfer by Private A/C Vehicle to<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><strong> Alexandria</strong></span> where it` is 225 k/m away from Cairo.</p>\r\n<p>Arrive&nbsp; at Alexandria around 10 am and start your tour there by Visiting <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">the Catacomb or Kom El-Shoqafa Tombs</span>(Tombs on three levels, also contains the Banquet hall where relatives used to sit on stone benches to have their meals catacombs tombs were decorated with relieves of bearded serpents and Inside are 2nd Century AD statues of Anubis wearing Roman Armor) Then visit <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">pompays pillar </span>then move to visit t<span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">he New library of Alexandria</span> the biggest library in the world now with 8 million books, then after lunch which is included at a Local Restaurant Based on Full Meal for each Person but Beverages are not included you will move to visit <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Qaytbay Citadel </span>a15th-century A d fortress located on the Mediterraneansea coast. It was established in 1477 AD by Sultan Al-Ashraf Qa&rsquo;it Bay.</p>\r\n<p>The Citadel is situated on the same place of the <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Pharaohs </span>or <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">the lighthouse of Alexandria</span> &amp;<span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">El Mursi Abu Elabas mosque </span>where you can have a free walk on the Cornish.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;Finally our Tour guide will drop you off at your hotel in Cairo you will be back to Cairo around 17:00 pm.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to the day tour as like:</strong><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/fascinating-cairo-dinner-cruise-on-nile/\">Cairo Dinner Cruise</a>.<br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/sound-and-light-show-at-giza-pyramids/\">Sound and Light Show at Giza Pyramids</a>.<br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/tour-to-wekalet-el-ghoury-for-tanoura-egyptian-heritage-dance-show/\">Al Tannoura Egyptian Heritage Show at Wekalet El Ghory</a>&nbsp;.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-divider-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-mgb gdlr-core-divider-item-normal gdlr-core-center-align\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div id=\"map\" class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper \" data-skin=\"Blue Icon\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-content gdlr-core-js \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-container clearfix gdlr-core-container\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<div class=\"mapouter\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(111, 'day', 'Luxor Day trip from Sharm el Sheikh by plane', 'Luxor / Sharm', '1789271761_tour.jpg', 105.00, 210.00, 105.00, '15 Hours', '6:00AM', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item gdlr-core-item-pdb clearfix  gdlr-core-left-align gdlr-core-title-item-caption-bottom gdlr-core-item-pdlr\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title-wrap\">\r\n<h6 class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title gdlr-core-skin-title\">Tour Details</h6>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>&nbsp;Tour Approx. 15 Hours Runs Every Day from 05:00 AM to 08:00 PM, Private Tour includes Pick up services from your hotel in Sharm and return, All transfers by a private A/C vehicle, Private Licensed Egyptologist guide, Bottle of water, All service charges &amp; taxes and Domestic Flight Tickets Sharm/Luxor/Sharm, Tour excludes tipping and Any extras not mentioned in the itinerary</p>\r\n<p><strong>There is possibility to visit the tomb of king tutankhamon, horse carriage ride in the cornichst of luxor&nbsp; or&nbsp; hot air balloon &nbsp;but all those Excursion can be added on in the middle of the tour with your guide</strong></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Domestic flights</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Unscheduled stops</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<div id=\"itinerary\" class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-content gdlr-core-js \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-container clearfix gdlr-core-container\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>Our representative At 5:00 am will Pick you up from your Hotel to Cairo Airport then at Luxor Airport you will meet our professional tour Guide then you will be transferred by Private A/C Vehicle to the <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>West Bank of Luxor</strong> </span>where you will visit the<span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"> V<em>alley Of The Kings</em></span>, the magnificence of the grandeur of architecture which was used for burial where there are many kings were buried in this valley.</p>\r\n<p>The most known tombs are King Tutmosis I, Tutmosis III, Tut-Ankh-Amon, King Ramssess VI, King Mrenptah and AmonhotepII.<br>Followed by a visit to t<span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">he Temple of Queen Hatshepsut</span> that known as El Dir El Bahari which was built by the 1st woman who was called Queen Hatshepsut the daughter of Thutmosis I, ruled Egypt about 20 years during the 18th Dynasty (approximately 1490-1469 B.C),<br>Then continue your day Tour to<span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"> The Colossi of Memnon</span> which is remains of the mortuary temple of Amenhotep III.</p>\r\n<p>Lunch Break at Local Restaurants<br>Then Transfer to the<span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong> East Bank of Luxor </strong></span>visits in Luxor to continue your day Tour visiting <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Karnak Temple</span>, the greatest example of worship in the history, dedicated to the main triad of Luxor (God Amon, his wife Mut and their son Khonsu).</p>\r\n<p>Finish your day tour by visiting <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">the Temple Of Luxor</span>, it was built by Amunhotep III in 18th Dynasty in the New Kingdom and it was completed by Ramses&rsquo; II during the 19th Dynasty.<br>Later you will be driven back to Luxor Airport.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to the day tour as like:</strong><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/sound-and-light-show-at-karnak-temple-in-luxor/\">Sound and Light Show at Karnak Temple</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/luxor-city-tour-on-horse-carriage/\">Luxor City tour on Horse Carriage&nbsp;</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/felucca-ride-on-the-nile-in-luxor/\">Short felucca ride on the Nile River</a></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-divider-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-mgb gdlr-core-divider-item-normal gdlr-core-center-align\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div id=\"map\" class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper \" data-skin=\"Blue Icon\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-content gdlr-core-js \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-container clearfix gdlr-core-container\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>'),
(113, 'half', 'Luxor City tour on Horse Carriage', 'Luxor', '1789269996_tour.jpg', 45.00, 65.00, 45.00, '2 Hours', 'before midnight', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Private Tour for 2 Hours Runs Daily as Per Request time, Private trip includes Expert Tour guide, All Taxes &amp; Services and All Pickup and drop off transfers,riding fees for the horse carriage, Bottle of water for each during your tour,tour excludes any extras and Tipping.</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\">1-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">2-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">3-&nbsp;&nbsp;All Transfers as mentioned.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\">4- bottle of water for each person</p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>As Per Requested time our professional tour guide will pick you up from your hotel or Nile Cruise in Luxor Then get on a private Horse Carriage where you can have a free walk over the Nile Cornish to explore the real life of Egyptian in Luxor.<br>At the end of the Tour you will be Transferred Back to your Hotel or Nile Cruise in Luxor.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to this tour like:</strong></p>\r\n<p>1- Sound and Light Show at karnakTemple.<br>2- Dinner at one of the local restaurants<br>3- Short felucca ride on the Nile River</p>'),
