span>, the magnificence of the grandeur of architecture which was used for burial where there are many kings were buried in this valley.<br>The most known tombs are King Tutmosis I, Tutmosis III, Tut-Ankh-Amon, King Ramssess VI, King Mrenptah and AmonhotepII.<br>Followed by a visit to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">the Temple of Queen Hatshepsut</span> that known as El Dir El Bahari which was built by the 1st woman who was called Queen Hatshepsut the daughter of Thutmosis I, ruled Egypt about 20 years during the 18th Dynasty (approximately 1490-1469 B.C),<br>Then continue your day Tour to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">The Colossi of Memnon</span> which is remains of the mortuary temple of Amenhotep III.<br>Lunch Break at Local Restaurants<br>Then Transfer to the<span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong> East Bank</strong></span> visits in Luxor to continue your day Tour visiting <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Karnak Temple,</span> the greatest example of worship in the history, dedicated to the main triad of Luxor (God Amon, his wife Mut and their son Khonsu ).<br>Finish your day tour by visiting <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">the Temple Of Luxor</span>, it was built by Amunhotep III in 18th Dynasty in the New Kingdom and it was completed by Ramses&rsquo; II during the 19th Dynasty.<br>Later you will be driven back to Luxor Airport.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>');
