ast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">lunch</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>&nbsp;Our professional tour guide At 7:00 am will Pick you up from your Hotel or Nile Cruise in Luxor then you will be transferred by Private A/C Vehicle to the West Bank where you will visit the Valley Of The Kings, the magnificence of the grandeur of architecture which was used for burial where there are many kings were buried in this valley.<br>The most known tombs are King Tutmosis I, Tutmosis III, Tut-Ankh-Amon, King Ramssess VI, King Mrenptah and AmonhotepII.<br>Followed by a visit to the Temple of Queen Hatshepsut that known as El Dir El Bahari which was built by the 1st woman who was called Queen Hatshepsut the daughter of Thutmosis I, ruled Egypt about 20 years during the 18th Dynasty (approximately 1490-1469 B.C),<br>Then continue your day Tour to The Colossi of Memnon which is remains of the mortuary temple of Amenhotep III.<br>Lunch Break at Local Restaurants<br>Then Transfer to the East Bank visits in Luxor to continue your day Tour visiting Karnak Temple, the greatest example of worship in the history, dedicated to the main triad of Luxor (God Amon, his wife Mut and their son Khonsu ).<br>Finish your day tour by visiting the Temple Of Luxor, it was built by Amunhotep III in 18th Dynasty in the New Kingdom and it was completed by Ramses&rsquo; II during the 19th Dynasty.<br>Later you will be driven back to your hotel in Luxor.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to the day tour as like:</strong><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/sound-and-light-show-at-karnak-temple-in-luxor/\">Sound and Light Show at Karnak Temple</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/luxor-city-tour-on-horse-carriage/\">Luxor City tour on Horse Carriage&nbsp;</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/felucca-ride-on-the-nile-in-luxor/\">Short felucca ride on the Nile River</a></p>'),
(116, 'half', 'Half Day Tour Visit Luxor Mummification Museum', 'Luxor', '1789269557_tour.jpg', 55.00, 75.00, 55.00, '4 Hours', 'any time before mid day', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Tour for 4 Hours Runs Every Day at 10 am, private tour includes Pick up services from hotel in Luxor and return, Entry Fees, Expert Tour guide, All Taxes Services, Bottle of Water and All Transfers by Private A/C Vehicle Newest Model, Tour excludes Personal Items and There is possibility to, horse carriage ride in the cornich st of Luxor or hot air balloon or short felucca ride on the but all those Excursion can be added on in the middle of the tour with your guide</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">1-</span><span style=\"font-size: 7.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">2-</span><span style=\"font-size: 7.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">3-</span><span style=\"font-size: 7.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">All Transfers as mentioned.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">4- bottle of water for each person</span></p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">lunch</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<div id=\"itinerary\" class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-content gdlr-core-js \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-container clearfix gdlr-core-container\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<p>Egypt travel square Expert tour guide At 10 am Pick you up from your Hotel to start your half day tour Visiting Luxor Museum and Mummification Museum Start by Luxor Museum where located in the Egyptian city of Luxor. It located on the corniche, overlooking the west bank of the Nile River.<br>It was opened in 1975, the museum is housed in a small, purpose-built building. The range of artifacts on display is far more restricted than the country&rsquo;s main collections in the Museum of Antiquities in Cairo; this was, however, deliberate, since the museum prides itself on the quality of the pieces it has, the uncluttered way in which they are displayed, and the clear multilingual labeling used.<br>Then move to Mummification museum It is located in the Egyptian city of Luxor. It stands on the corniche, in front of the Mina Palace Hotel, to the north of Luxor Temple, overlooking the River Nile<br>The museum is intended to provide visitors with an understanding of the ancient art of mummification. The Ancient Egyptians applied embalming techniques to many species, not only to dead humans. Mummies of cats, fish and crocodiles are on display in this unique museum, where one can also get an idea of the tools used.<br>Later Transfer Back to your Hotel in Luxor.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to the day tour as like:</strong><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/sound-and-light-show-at-karnak-temple-in-luxor/\">Sound and Light Show at Karnak Temple</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/luxor-city-tour-on-horse-carriage/\">Luxor City tour on Horse Carriage&nbsp;</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/felucca-ride-on-the-nile-in-luxor/\">Short felucca ride on the Nile River</a></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-divider-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-mgb gdlr-core-divider-item-normal gdlr-core-center-align\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div id=\"map\" class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper \" data-skin=\"Blue Icon\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-content gdlr-core-js \">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-wrapper-container clearfix gdlr-core-container\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item gdlr-core-item-pdb clearfix  gdlr-core-left-align gdlr-core-title-item-caption-bottom gdlr-core-item-pdlr\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title-wrap\">\r\n<h6 class=\"gdlr-core-title-item-title gdlr-core-skin-title\">&nbsp;</h6>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-pbf-element\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item gdlr-core-item-pdlr gdlr-core-item-pdb gdlr-core-left-align\">\r\n<div class=\"gdlr-core-text-box-item-content\">\r\n<div class=\"mapouter\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', ''),
(117, 'day', 'Tour to Madinet Habu temple and Dier el madina or Valley Of Workers', 'Luxor', '1789269445_tour.jpg', 85.00, 170.00, 85.00, '8 Hours', '8:00AM', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>Tour for 8 Hours Private Tour Runs daily from 8:00 am to 2:00 pm includes Pick up services from your hotel in Luxor and return, all transfers by a private A/C vehicle, Private English-speaking Egyptologist guide,Bottle of water for each during your tour and All service charges &amp; taxes, Tour excludes Any extras, Tipping and any Optional Tour</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">1-</span><span style=\"font-size: 7.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">2-</span><span style=\"font-size: 7.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">3-</span><span style=\"font-size: 7.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">All Transfers as mentioned.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">4- bottle of water for each person</span></p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Our professional tour Guide At 7:00 am Pick you up from your Hotel or Nile Cruise in Luxor then you will be transferred by Private A/C Vehicle to the West Bank of the Nile where you will visit Medinat Habu, it is an archaeological locality situated near the foot of the Theban Hills on the West Bank of the River Nile opposite the modern city of Luxor,<br>Also other structures are located within the area, the location is today associated almost exclusively with the Mortuary Temple of Ramses III The temple, some 150m long, is of orthodox design, and resembles closely the mortuary temple of Ramses II (the Ramseum temple ).<br>It is quite well preserved and surrounded by a massive mud brick enclosure, which may have been fortified. The original entrance is through a fortified gate-house, known as a migdol (and resembling an Asiatic fortress). The name at least its French form, Rhamess&eacute;ion &ndash; was coined by Jean-Fran&ccedil;ois Champollion, who visited the ruins of the site in 1829 and first identified the hieroglyphs making up Ramses&rsquo;s names and titles on the walls.<br>It was originally called the House of millions of years of Usermaatra-setepenra that unites with Thebes-the-city in the domain of Amon.<br>Also there are some other temples inside Habu Temple like Temple of Amun dating to the 18th Dynasty, built by Queen Hatshepsut and Thutmose III. It has undergone many alterations and modifications over the years, partially in the 20th, 25th, 26th, 29th and 30th Dynasties and the Greco-Roman period.<br>Then Continue your day Tour to Deir el Medina, known as The Valley of the worker or the City of the worker , Deir el-Medina is an ancient Egyptian village which was home to the artisans who worked on the tombs in the Valley of the Kings during the 18th to 20th dynasties of the New Kingdom period (ca. 1550&ndash;1080 BC) The paintings appear so fresh.<br>End your day Tour with a visit to Valley of the Queens it&rsquo;s is a place where wives of Pharaohs were buried in ancient times. In ancient times, it was known as Ta-Set-Neferu, meaning &ndash;&rdquo;the place of the Children of the Pharaoh&rdquo;, because along with the Queens of the 18th, 19th and 20th dynasties (1550&ndash;1070 BCE) many princes and princesses were also buried with various members of the nobility.<br>The tombs of these individuals were protected by funeral priests who performed daily rituals and provided offerings and prayers for the deceased nobility. The valley is located near the better known Valley of the Kings, on the west bank of the Nile across from Thebes (modernLuxor).<br>The kings of the 18th dynasty, instead of building pyramids as traditional burial chambers (perhaps because of their vulnerability to tomb robbers), now chose to be interred in rock-cut tombs to Preserve it as possible as they can from tomb robbers After that you will be moved to your hotel</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to the day tour as like:</strong><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/sound-and-light-show-at-karnak-temple-in-luxor/\">Sound and Light Show at Karnak Temple</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/luxor-city-tour-on-horse-carriage/\">Luxor City tour on Horse Carriage&nbsp;</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/felucca-ride-on-the-nile-in-luxor/\">Short felucca ride on the Nile River</a></p>'),
(118, 'package', 'Nile Cruise from Aswan to Luxor for 4 Days 3 Nights', 'Aswan / Luxor', '1789269245_tour.jpg', 1100.00, 1450.00, 1100.00, '4 Days 3 Nights', 'Every Saturday, Monday, Wednesday, Thursday & Friday from Aswan to Luxor', 'English, Spanish, German, French &italian', 'according to travellers dates', '<p>Nile Cruise trip sails Every Saturday, Monday, Wednesday, Thursday &amp; Friday from Aswan to Luxor for 4 Days 3 Nights, includes Meet and Assist upon arrival &amp; Departure, all transfers by Air Conditioned modern vehicles, Accommodation on full board basis, Meals as indicated in the Cruise itinerary, Egyptologist tour guide, Assistance and All service charges and taxes.</p>\r\n<p>There is possibility to visit the tomb of king Tutankhamon , hot air balloon in Luxor, riding camel Luxor or Aswan desert or ridding the quad bike at the wide desert or of both Luxor and Aswan but all those excursions can be added on the middle of the tour as it requires additional fees</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">1-</span><span style=\"font-size: 7.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">Transportation in private air-conditioned van.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">2-</span><span style=\"font-size: 7.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp; photographer.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">3-</span><span style=\"font-size: 7.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">All Transfers as mentioned.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; background: white; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: maroon;\">4- bottle of water for each person</span></p>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Entry Fees</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Personal Items</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Tipping</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">any Optional tours as entering any of the temples or tombs from Inside Requires additional ticket Can be added on</span></li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Booking confirmation</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">Comfortable shoes</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Day 1</span>:</strong>&nbsp;Transfer to Nile Cruise &amp; Aswan tours<br>Meet &amp; assist at Aswan airport, Railway station Or Hotel by our guide then<br>Transfer to your Nile Cruise. Check in at 12:00 pm<br>Lunch on board<br>Visit <strong><span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Aswan high dam</span> </strong>and <strong><span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Philae temple</span></strong><br><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Felucca ride on the Nile</span></strong><br>Dinner on board<br>Overnight in Aswan<br>Meals: <strong>Lunch, Dinner</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Day 2</span>:</strong>&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Kom-Ombo &amp; Edfu</span></strong><br><strong>Breakfast on board</strong><br>Sailing to Kom-Ombo<br>Visit <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\">Kom-Ombo temple</span> shared by two gods Sobek &amp; Haeroris<br>Sailing to Edfu<br><strong>Lunch on board</strong><br>Visit the <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong>temple of Horus at Edfu</strong></span><br>Sail to Luxor via Esna<br>Free time at leisure on Board<br>Afternoon tea on sun deck<br>Cross Esna lock<br><strong>Dinner on board</strong><br><strong>Galabiya party</strong><br>Meals:<strong> Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Day 3</span>:</strong>&nbsp;Visit <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Luxor east bank</span><br><strong>Breakfast on board</strong>.<br>Visit the <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Valley of the Kings</span>,<span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"> Queen Hatshepsut temple, and Colossi of Memnon</span><br>Transfer to Luxor hotel, airport or railway station<br><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Lunch on board</span><br><strong>Dinner on board</strong><br><strong>party &amp; Music in the evening</strong><br>Overnight in Luxor<br>Meals:<strong> Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Day 4</span>:</strong>&nbsp;Disembarkation, Visit<span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong> Luxor West Bank</strong></span> &ndash; Departure transfer<br>Breakfast on board.<br>Disembarkation after breakfast (08:00 am)<br>Visit <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Karnak temple &amp; Luxor temple</span></p>\r\n<p>N.B: Itinerary may change in sequence but not in visits. Egypt travel square is not liable for these changes</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to this tour like:</strong></p>\r\n<p>-Sound and Light Show at&nbsp;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/sound-and-light-show-at-karnak-temple-in-luxor/\">karnak</a>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/philae-temple-sound-and-light-show-aswan/\">Philae</a>&nbsp;Temple<br>-Carriage ridding in&nbsp;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/luxor-city-tour-on-horse-carriage/\">Luxor</a>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/aswan-city-tour-on-horse-carriage/\">Aswan</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/felucca-ride-on-the-nile-in-aswan/\">Short felucca ride in Aswan</a></p>'),
