p i<strong>nfront of&nbsp; Port Said or Alexandria port</strong> with a sign appearance your name on it then, at that point, move you to Cairo around 230 K/M from Port Said or Alexandria</p>\r\n<p>Arrival to Cairo start your day visit Visiting <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">the Great Pyramids Of Giza &ndash; Cheops, Chephren and Mykerinos </span>then Visit <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">the Valley Temple</span> The Place where the Priests Mummified the dead group of lord Chephren proprietor of the second pyramid at Giza Platue Also it&rsquo;s a similar spot where you Can have a nearby glance at <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">the Sphinx</span> &ndash; The incredible watchman that stands by the immense burial service complex with its lion body and the head of ruler Chephren. Lunch is remembered for between visits at Local Restaurant Based on Full Meal for every Person except Beverages are excluded Then Continue your day visit to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Sakkara</span>, found just 27 km southwest away from Cairo. Visit the Step Pyramid (Built for ruler Zoser), it is viewed as a significant part during the time spent the pyramid advancement, which were produced using the straightforward mastaba to its commonly known structure. Then proceed with your day visit to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\">Memphis</span>, the old capital of Egypt, where the goliath sculpture of Ramses II and the incomparable Alabaster Sphinx are. This City Dates back to 3100 B.C, An Optional shopping visit at the conventional markets where you can buy a scope of customary keepsakes, for example, scent oils, papyrus, hieroglyphics in various materials and so on<br>Toward the finish of the visit you will be moved to your Hotel Check in and Overnight in Cairo&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h4 class=\"gdlr-core-toggle-box-item-title gdlr-core-js  gdlr-core-skin-e-background gdlr-core-skin-e-content\"><span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><span class=\"gdlr-core-h