 auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Camera</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun glasses</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">sun block</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\">hat</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in;\">Passport</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Our professional tour guide At 6:00 Am or 7:00 Am will Pick you up from your Hotel or Nile Cruise in Aswan then you will be transferred by Private A/C Vehicle to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Luxor </strong></span>then go directly to the West Bank where you will visit <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong>the Valley Of The Kings</strong></span>, the magnificence of the grandeur of architecture which was used for burial where there are many kings were buried in this valley.<br>The most known tombs are King Tutmosis I, Tutmosis III, Tut-Ankh-Amon, King Ramssess VI, King Mrenptah and AmonhotepII.<br>Followed by a visit to<span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong> the Temple of Queen Hatshepsut</strong></span> that known as El Dir El Bahari which was built by the 1st woman who was called Queen Hatshepsut the daughter of Thutmosis I, ruled Egypt about 20 years during the 18th Dynasty (approximately 1490-1469 B.C),<br>Then continue your day Tour to <span style=\"color: rgb(186, 55, 42);\"><strong>The Colossi of Memnon</strong></span> which is remains of the mortuary temple of Amenhotep III.<br>Lunch Break at Local Restaurants<br>Then Transfer to <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>the East Bank </strong></span>visits in Luxor to continue your day Tour visiting <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>Karnak Temple</strong></span>, the greatest example of worship in the history, dedicated to the main triad of Luxor (God Amon, his wife Mut and their son Khonsu).<br>Finish your day tour by visiting <span style=\"color: rgb(224, 62, 45);\"><strong>the Temple Of Luxor</strong></span>, it was built by Amunhotep III in 18th Dynasty in the New Kingdom and it was completed by Ramses&rsquo; II during the 19th Dynasty.<br>Later you will be driven back to your hotel in Aswan.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Also you can add a night tour to the day tour as like:</strong><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/sound-and-light-show-at-karnak-temple-in-luxor/\">Sound and Light Show at Karnak Temple</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/luxor-city-tour-on-horse-carriage/\">Luxor City tour on Horse Carriage&nbsp;</a><br>&ndash;<a href=\"https://egyptsquaretemp-com.stackstaging.com/tour/felucca-ride-on-the-nile-in-luxor/\">Short felucca ride on the Nile River</a></p>'),
(150, 'day', ' Al-Alamein Day tour  from Alexandria', 'Alexandria', '1789347123_tour.jpg', 95.00, 190.00, 95.00, 'Full Day', '8:00AM', 'English, Spanish, German, French', 'Runs on a daily basis', '<p>starts every day at 8:00 am for 5 Hours, Private tour includes, pick up service from your hotel in Alexandria and return, Professional English-speaking tour guide, all transfers by a modern A/C vehicle, (Bottle of water) and All service charges &amp; taxes, Tour excludes Personal expenses, tipping and Optional activities.</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpFirst\" style=\"mso-add-space: auto; text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; color: maroon;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">1-<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; color: maroon;\">Transportation in private air-conditioned van. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormalCxSpMiddle\" style=\"mso-add-space: auto; text-indent: -.25in; line-height: normal; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in 0in .0001pt .25in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; color: maroon;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">2-<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; mso-bidi-font-family: \'Comic Sans MS\'; color: maroon;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;</span>Private Professional English Speaking tour guide &amp;